// This example is interesting because an older version of the infer result pass actually
// added two assignments to gather results from terminal expression.
//
// Nested assignment of temporaries like `t#0 = t#1 = i < 3` should not make it to later
// stages.
//
// The generate code stage needs to unnest this assignment before the TmpL backend can
// translate it.  If the TmpL backend were to try to handle this by creating temporaries,
// those would miss type information.
var i = 0;
while (i < 3) { ++i; }
